 ##
+# @x-fdisbull-arm-display-motion:
+#
+# @token: Unused input owner token of 1..128 bytes.
+# @dx: QEMU relative X count in -127..127, positive right.
+# @dy: QEMU relative Y count in -127..127, positive down.
+# @expected: Exact stopped publication and configuration expectation.
+#
+# Passively arm one nonzero relative-motion pair for 2 ms after acceptance.
+# Requires prior precise VGA admission, a stopped nonempty retained display
+# window, and matching current/published configuration generation and raw
+# values.  Every expected field must match one fresh full owned observation.
+# Neither guest pointer scale nor pixel arithmetic is inferred by this command.
+#
+# Native code prepares only nonzero X then nonzero Y events as one owned PS/2
+# batch.  At the deadline, stop and reached/equal clock-budget precedence run
+# before a fresh publication/configuration guard and selected-handler checks.
+# Impossible history fails before choosing configuration-change precedence
+# among valid binding changes.  A valid change cancels without any relative
+# callback; regressed or contradictory identity fails.  No guard failure
+# refreshes the display, rebases a request,
+# retries an event or consumes a new token.  The first actual VM stop consumes
+# an unfired attempt.  Completion does not stop the guest.
+#
+# Shares query/cancel, migration restriction and token history.  Accepted
+# arms clear other plan descriptors; other accepted arms clear motion.
+# Rejected arms preserve the preceding receipt and do not consume the token.
+# The host must retain a cancelled mapped plan's binding until explicit
+# cancellation; it must not convert those pending records to an ordinary or
+# retrace arm.  Independently requested lower-level input keeps its contract.
+#
+# No button event is requested.  Existing buttons, residual motion and device
+# mode are not neutralized.  Device FIFO acceptance, guest consumption,
+# actual pixel displacement and cursor position remain unknown.
+#
+# Returns: Armed receipt with immutable full binding evidence.
+#
+# Since: 10.0
+##
+{ 'command': 'x-fdisbull-arm-display-motion',
+  'data': { 'token': 'str', 'dx': 'int', 'dy': 'int',
+            'expected': 'FdisbullDisplayMotionExpected' },
+  'returns': 'FdisbullInputInfo' }
+
